5</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib6"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Fountoulakis</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Langen</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Identification of proteins by matrix-assisted laser desorption ionization-mass spectrometry following in-gel digestion in low-salt, nonvolatile buffer and simplified peptide recovery</article-title><source>Anal Biochem</source><year>1997</year><volume>250</volume><fpage>153</fpage><lpage>156</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Anal Biochem||250|153||bib6|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9245432</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gerner</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Holzmann</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Grimm</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Sauermann</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Similarity between nuclear matrix proteins of various cells revealed by an improved isolation method</article-title><source>J Cell Biochem</source><year>1998</year><volume>71</volume><fpage>363</fpage><lpage>374</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'J Cell Biochem||71|363||bib7|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9831073</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Grasl-Kraupp</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Bursch</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Ruttkay-Nedecky</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Wagner</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Lauer</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Schulte-Hermann</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Food restriction eliminates 